        <zone h='80000' id='22' type-v2='text' w='37000' x='62000' y='10500'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1a1a1a' fontname='Arial' fontsize='14'>Full test: all municipalities&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#5a5f6e' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='11'>879 one-year-ahead predictions for 226 municipalities, made before the real rents were published.

</run>
            <run fontcolor='#5a5f6e' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='11'>Average error&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1a1a1a' fontname='Arial' fontsize='26'>€0.32/m²</run>
            <run fontcolor='#5a5f6e' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>  (about 6% of the rent)&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1a1a1a' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>Compared with simple rules (average error, €/m²)
</run>
            <run fontcolor='#5a5f6e' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='11'>• Model (tuned gradient boosting): €0.322
</run>
            <run fontcolor='#5a5f6e' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='11'>• Every rent grows by the average rate: €0.305
</run>
            <run fontcolor='#5a5f6e' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='11'>• Rent stays the same: €0.567&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1a1a1a' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>Spotting the fastest-growing 20%
</run>
            <run fontcolor='#5a5f6e' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='11'>• When the model says &quot;top 20%&quot;, it is right 38% of the time (random guess: 20%)
• Confusion matrix: 65 right picks · 108 false alarms · 109 missed · 597 correct &quot;not top&quot;

</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1a1a1a' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>Average error by area&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#5a5f6e' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='11'>• Lisbon area €0.44 · Porto area €0.30 · Rest of Portugal €0.31

</run>
            <run fontcolor='#5a5f6e' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='11'>Chart colours: </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#c87b29' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='11'>Lisbon area</run>
            <run fontcolor='#5a5f6e' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='11'> · </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#404f7a' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='11'>Porto area</run>
            <run fontcolor='#5a5f6e' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='11'> · </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#8d9dbe' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='11'>Rest of Portugal</run>
            <run fontcolor='#5a5f6e' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='11'> · grey line = perfect prediction</run>
          </formatted-text>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#d7d6db' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='solid' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='1' />
            <format attr='margin' value='4' />
            <format attr='padding' value='14' />
            <format attr='background-color' value='#ffffff' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
        <zone h='7500' id='20' type-v2='text' w='98000' x='1000' y='91500'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1a1a1a' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='11'>Note: </run>
            <run fontcolor='#5a5f6e' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='11'>The summary on the right covers the full test (notebook 02). The chart follows the filters above, which are shared with the 2027 outlook tab. All accuracy figures come from this historical test; the 2027 figures are estimates and cannot be checked yet.</run>
          </formatted-text>
